    <string name="notation_intro_header_title">Introduction</string>
    <string name="notation_intro_header_body">Guide to information about the notation used in this app.\n\nNotation cited in this section can be used as reference for solves, provide more information and give a better understanding of the puzzle.\n\nAt the moment all information given will only relate to the 3x3x3 Rubiks cube</string>
    <string name="notation_intro_gestures_hint">Swipe Right to Left for more tabs and notation information</string>

    <string name="notation_faces_header_title">Explanation of Faces:</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_header_body">On a standard 3x3x3 Cube there are 6 faces.\n\nThese 6 faces are named and used depending non the colour which is facing you.</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_left">The Left face\nThe face to the left of you</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_right">The Right face\nThe face to the right of you</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_front">The Front face\nThe face at the front of the cube</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_back">The Back face\nThe face at the back of the cube</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_up">The Up Face\nThe face at the top of the cube</string>
    <string name="notation_faces_down">The Down face\nThe face at the bottom of the cube</string>

    <string name="notation_moves_header_title">Explanation of Moves</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_header_body">These moves will be listed as clockwise moves and anticlockwise moves\n\n Clockwise moves are noted with a capital letter for the face e.g. R.\n\n Anticlockwise moves are noted with a capital letter for the face and an apostrophe e.g. R\'</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_clockwise_r">Right clockwise: R\nClockwise turn of the right layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_anticlockwise_r">Right Anti-clockwise: R\'\nAnti Clockwise turn of the right layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_clockwise_l">Left clockwise: L\nClockwise turn of the left layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_anticlockwise_l">Left Anti-clockwise: L\'\nAnti Clockwise turn of the left layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_clockwise_u">Up clockwise: U\nClockwise turn of the up layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_anticlockwise_u">Up Anti-clockwise: U\'\nAnti Clockwise turn of the up layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_clockwise_d">Down clockwise: D\nClockwise turn of the down layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_anticlockwise_d">Down Anti-clockwise: D\'\nAnti Clockwise turn of the down layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_clockwise_f">Front clockwise: F\nClockwise turn of the front layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_anticlockwise_f">Front Anti-clockwise: F\'\nAnti Clockwise turn of the front layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_clockwise_b">Back clockwise: B\nClockwise turn of the back layer</string>
    <string name="notation_moves_anticlockwise_b">Back Anti-clockwise: B\'\nAnti Clockwise turn of the back layer</string>

    <string name="notation_doubles_header_title">Double Moves</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_header_body">Double layer moves will be noted as a capital Letter and number 2 e.g. R2</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_r">Double R Move: R2\n\nDouble turn in one direction on the right face</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_l">Double L Move: L2\n\nDouble turn in one direction on the left face</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_u">Double U Move: U2\n\nDouble turn in one direction on the up face</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_d">Double D Move: D2\n\nDouble turn in one direction on the down face</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_f">Double F Move: F2\n\nDouble turn in one direction on the front face</string>
    <string name="notation_doubles_b">Double B Move: B2\n\nDouble turn in one direction on the back face</string>

    <string name="notation_two_layer_header_title">Explanation of 2-Layer Moves:</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_header_body">In more complex algorithms there is a need for 2 layers to be turned simultaneously these moves are denoted with a lower case letter.\n\nThey can be accessed on the Algorithm keyboard these can be accessed by clicking on the shift button</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_r">2-Layer r Move: r\n\nTurn the right and front vertical layer 90 degrees</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_l">2-Layer l Move: l\n\nTurn the left and front vertical layer 90 degrees</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_u">2-Layer u Move: u\n\nTurn the up and front horizontal layer 90 degrees</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_d">2-Layer d Move: d\n\nTurn the down and front horizontal layer 90 degrees</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_f">2-Layer f Move: f\n\nTurn the front and right vertical middle layer 90 degrees</string>
    <string name="notation_two_layer_b">2-Layer b Move: b\n\nTurn the back and right vertical middle layer 90 degrees</string>

    <string name="notation_slices_header_title">Explanation of Slice moves:</string>
    <string name="notation_slices_header_body">Slice moves are moves made with layers in between diagonally opposite faces.\n\nThese moves are not seen as often in algorithms but are still seen.</string>
    <string name="notation_slices_m">Middle Layer Slice: M\n\nLayers between the Right and Left layers</string>
    <string name="notation_slices_e">E-Layer Slice: E\n\nLayers between the Up and Down layers</string>
    <string name="notation_slices_s">S Layer Slice: S\n\nLayers between the Front and Back layers</string>
    <string name="notation_slices_extra_header">Extra Information:</string>
    <string name="notation_slices_extra_body">Anti clockwise slices are noted with the slice move followed by an apostrophe e.g. M\'\n\n Double slice moves are noted with the slice move followed by the number 2 e.g. M2</string>

    <string name="notation_rotations_header_title">Explanation of Rotations:</string>
    <string name="notation_rotations_header_body">Explanation for the rotations that can be used within a solve on the standard 3x3x3 Rubik\'s cube</string>
    <string name="notation_rotations_x">X axis Rotation: X\n\nRotating the cube clockwise on the X-axis e.g. the Front face will become the Up face</string>
    <string name="notation_rotations_y">Y axis Rotation: Y\n\nRotating the cube clockwise on the Y-axis e.g. the Front face will become the Left face</string>
    <string name="notation_rotations_z">Z axis Rotation: Z\n\nRotating the cube clockwise on the Z-axis e.g. the Up face will become the Right face</string>
    <string name="notation_rotations_extra_header">Extra Information:</string>
    <string name="notation_rotations_extra_body">Anti clockwise rotations are noted with the rotation move followed by an apostrophe e.g. X\'\n\n Double rotations are noted with the rotation move followed by the number 2 e.g. X2</string>

    <string name="notation_algorithms_header_title">How Algorithms Work</string>
    <string name="notation_algorithms_header_body">Algorithms are made up of Moves, Slices and Rotations performed one after another.\n\nAlgorithms are noted down with commas between the moves and sometimes brackets used to separate up chunks of algorithms</string>
    <!-- endregion -->

